    <!-- FAQ & Changelog Tab -->
    <string name="faq_title">FAQ &amp; Changelog</string>
    <string name="faq_q0">What is new in version 1.5.0?</string>
    <string name="faq_a0">1. Vector Framework &amp; LibXposed API 102 priority: native XposedService + RemotePreferences sync allows changing settings and custom curves in real time WITHOUT requiring Root IPC (while preserving full SystemProperties fallback for legacy LSPosed forks).\n2. Fixed Active Protection Statistics card: the module now emits throttled GUARD_STATS telemetry snapshots and pins BLOCKED / GUARD_STATS lines across long uptimes, showing both sleep-reset blocks and active protection events (Anti-Drift, Floor/DarkEnv, Custom Curve, Stability/Hysteresis).\n3. Improved UI layout &amp; OLED palette: unified Status + Protection card, grouped Settings, moved Device Compatibility to Tools, and made terminal commands collapsible.</string>
    <string name="faq_q1">What is the OxygenOS / ColorOS auto-brightness bug?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">On OnePlus / OPPO devices (OxygenOS / ColorOS 12–17), OplusAutomaticBrightnessController schedules an AlarmManager timer (usually 10 minutes) when the screen turns off. When triggered, resetAutoBrightness() (or resetAutoBrightness(1) with DragOpt on ColorOS 17) and OplusBrightnessAmbientAdapter.resetAmbientAdapter("AutoReset") erase your learned brightness curve.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">How do Vector Framework and KSUN + SUSFS work together?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">This module communicates with Vector Framework directly via Binder (LibXposed RemotePreferences &amp; XposedService) for live settings and scope status without calling su. Root access (KSUN, Magisk, APatch) is only needed inside the app when reading log files, dumpsys display panel calibration, or running Soft Reboot — compatible with SUSFS hiding.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">Is a reboot required after updating or changing settings?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">Changing toggles, minimum floor, sensor switches, or custom curve points applies INSTANTLY with zero reboot. Only upgrading the module APK (when hook code changes inside system_server) requires a 5-second Soft Reboot (available in Tools) or full reboot.</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">Does the module increase battery drain?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">No. Hardware light sensors and brightness observers register strictly while the app is open on screen (ON_RESUME / ON_PAUSE). Disabled sensors (MAIN / AUX / PWM) unsubscribe completely. Hooks inside system_server allocate zero background threads or timers and throttle stats logging to at most once every 60 seconds when counts change.</string>
